  </div>
</nav>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ OVERVIEW -->
<main class="main">
<section class="section active" id="tab-overview">

  <div class="hero">
    <div class="hero-tag">EMA GOOD VIGILANCE PRACTICE · MODULE IX</div>
    <h1>Signal Management<br><span>in Pharmacovigilance</span></h1>
    <p>A structured framework for detecting, validating, confirming, analysing, prioritising and recommending action on new safety information from pharmacovigilance data sources.</p>
    <div class="hero-chips">
      <div class="chip">EUDRAVIGILANCE</div>
      <div class="chip">ICSR ANALYSIS</div>
      <div class="chip">DISPROPORTIONALITY</div>
      <div class="chip">PSUR / PBRER</div>
      <div class="chip">RMP INTEGRATION</div>
      <div class="chip">PRAC REVIEW</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Legal Basis & Scope</div>
  <div class="section-h2">What is GVP Module IX?</div>
  <div class="section-desc">GVP Module IX describes the process obligations for MAHs and NCAs to detect and manage signals from all sources of pharmacovigilance data. Updated July 2023 — integrates new obligations from Implementing Regulation (EU) 520/2012.</div>

  <div class="grid-4">
    <div class="card card-accent">
      <h3><span class="icon">🎯</span>Signal</h3>
      <p>Information from one or more sources suggesting a new potentially causal association, or a new aspect of a known association, between an intervention and an event that is judged to be of sufficient likelihood to justify verificatory action.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card card-warn">
      <h3><span class="icon">⚠️</span>Important Identified Risk</h3>
      <p>An untoward occurrence for which there is adequate evidence of an association with the medicinal product of interest and which is of significance to public health or patient safety.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card card-green">
      <h3><span class="icon">🔍</span>Important Potential Risk</h3>
      <p>An untoward occurrence for which there is some basis for suspicion of an association with the medicinal product of interest but this association has not been confirmed.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card card-orange">
      <h3><span class="icon">📊</span>Missing Information</h3>
      <p>Gaps in knowledge about a medicinal product, for a specific safety issue or a population who may use the product, that could be relevant for public health.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>📋 Regulatory Framework</h3>
      <div class="toggle-item">
        <div class="toggle-head" onclick="tog(this)">Directive 2001/83/EC (as amended) <span class="chevron">▼</span></div>
        <div class="toggle-body">Articles 23a, 23b, 24 — obligations on MAH for signal detection. Article 107h — NCA national signal detection obligations.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="toggle-item">
        <div class="toggle-head" onclick="tog(this)">Regulation (EU) 536/2014 <span class="chevron">▼</span></div>
        <div class="toggle-body">Clinical trials pharmacovigilance integration with post-authorisation signal management.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="toggle-item">
        <div class="toggle-head" onclick="tog(this)">Implementing Regulation (EU) 520/2012 <span class="chevron">▼</span></div>
        <div class="toggle-body">Art. 19–24 detail the specific signal detection, validation and assessment requirements including EudraVigilance access obligations.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="toggle-item">
        <div class="toggle-head" onclick="tog(this)">ICH E2C(R2) / E2D / E2E <span class="chevron">▼</span></div>
        <div class="toggle-body">International harmonisation standards referenced for signal methodology, PSUR content, and post-authorisation safety study triggers.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>🏗️ Module IX Scope — Key Obligations</h3>
      <div class="prog-row">
        <div class="prog-label"><span>Signal Detection (All Sources)</span><span>MAH + NCA</span></div>
