<section class="section" id="tab-process">

  <div class="section-title">Step-by-Step Process</div>
  <div class="section-h2">The 5-Step Signal Management Process</div>
  <div class="section-desc">GVP Module IX defines five mandatory sequential activities. Click each step to expand detailed operational instructions.</div>

  <div class="process-flow">
    <div class="pf-step active-step" onclick="selectStep(0)">
      <div class="pf-arrow">▶</div>
      <div class="pf-num">STEP 01</div>
      <div class="pf-label">Signal Detection</div>
      <div class="pf-sub">Ongoing monitoring</div>
    </div>
    <div class="pf-step" onclick="selectStep(1)">
      <div class="pf-arrow">▶</div>
      <div class="pf-num">STEP 02</div>
      <div class="pf-label">Signal Validation</div>
      <div class="pf-sub">30-day window</div>
    </div>
    <div class="pf-step" onclick="selectStep(2)">
      <div class="pf-arrow">▶</div>
      <div class="pf-num">STEP 03</div>
      <div class="pf-label">Signal Confirmation</div>
      <div class="pf-sub">NCA / PRAC</div>
    </div>
    <div class="pf-step" onclick="selectStep(3)">
      <div class="pf-arrow">▶</div>
      <div class="pf-num">STEP 04</div>
      <div class="pf-label">Signal Assessment</div>
      <div class="pf-sub">Causality & impact</div>
    </div>
    <div class="pf-step" onclick="selectStep(4)">
      <div class="pf-num">STEP 05</div>
      <div class="pf-label">Recommendation & Action</div>
      <div class="pf-sub">Regulatory outcome</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step-detail visible" id="detail-0">
    <h3>Step 01 — Signal Detection</h3>
    <div class="sub">RESPONSIBILITY: MAH Pharmacovigilance Department + QPPV</div>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div>
        <div class="alert alert-info">
          <span class="icon">🔭</span>
          <div><strong>Definition:</strong> Signal detection is the systematic review of incoming data from all sources to identify new safety information that may require further evaluation.</div>
        </div>
        <h4 style="color:var(--accent);font-size:13px;margin:14px 0 8px;">Key Detection Methods</h4>
        <div class="toggle-item">
          <div class="toggle-head" onclick="tog(this)">Quantitative Signal Detection (QSD) — Disproportionality Analysis <span class="chevron">▼</span></div>
          <div class="toggle-body">
            <p>Compares observed vs. expected reporting rates using statistical measures:</p>
            <ul style="margin:8px 0 0 16px;color:var(--text-muted);">
              <li><strong style="color:var(--text)">PRR</strong> — Proportional Reporting Ratio (UK MHRA method)</li>
              <li><strong style="color:var(--text)">ROR</strong> — Reporting Odds Ratio</li>
              <li><strong style="color:var(--text)">EBGM / EB05</strong> — Empirical Bayes Geometric Mean (FDA FAERS)</li>
              <li><strong style="color:var(--text)">IC / IC025</strong> — Information Component (WHO VigiBase)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="toggle-item">
          <div class="toggle-head" onclick="tog(this)">Qualitative Signal Detection <span class="chevron">▼</span></div>
          <div class="toggle-body">Review of individual case narratives, medical literature reviews, clinical expert assessment. Mandatory for cases with fatal outcome, unlabelled serious ADRs, or cases in special populations.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="toggle-item">
          <div class="toggle-head" onclick="tog(this)">Literature Monitoring <span class="chevron">▼</span></div>
          <div class="toggle-body">Weekly systematic searches of PubMed / EMBASE / Cochrane. Search strategy should cover active substance, related compounds, and known MedDRA terms. All relevant articles must be assessed within 15 calendar days.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4 style="color:var(--accent);font-size:13px;margin:0 0 12px;">EudraVigilance Monitoring — Operational Steps</h4>
        <div class="timeline">
          <div class="tl-item">
            <div class="tl-left"><div class="tl-dot"></div><div class="tl-line"></div></div>
            <div class="tl-content">
              <div class="tl-date">DAY 1 — Login & Query Setup</div>
              <h4>Access EV Web Trader / E2B Gateway</h4>
              <p>Query by active substance (MedDRA PT/HLT/SOC) for target signal. Set date range for monitoring period.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <div class="tl-left"><div class="tl-dot warn"></div><div class="tl-line"></div></div>
            <div class="tl-content">
              <div class="tl-date">DAY 1-2 — Run QSD Metrics</div>
              <h4>Calculate PRR / ROR / EBGM</h4>
              <p>Apply thresholds: PRR ≥2, N ≥3, χ²≥4 (Evans method) to flag signals. Document all calculations.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <div class="tl-left"><div class="tl-dot warn"></div><div class="tl-line"></div></div>
            <div class="tl-content">
              <div class="tl-date">DAY 2-5 — Case Review</div>
              <h4>Individual Case Assessment</h4>
              <p>Review all flagged cases individually. Assess for completeness, seriousness, imputability, time-to-onset, dose, dechallenge/rechallenge.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <div class="tl-left"><div class="tl-dot green"></div></div>
            <div class="tl-content">
              <div class="tl-date">DAY 5-7 — Documentation</div>
              <h4>Signal Detection Log Update</h4>
              <p>Record all evaluated drug-event combinations, QSD values, conclusion (signal / not-a-signal), and next review date in the Safety Signal Log (SST/SML).</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step-detail" id="detail-1">
    <h3>Step 02 — Signal Validation</h3>
    <div class="sub">RESPONSIBILITY: MAH QPPV | DEADLINE: Within 30 calendar days of detection</div>
    <div class="alert alert-warn">
      <span class="icon">⏱️</span>
      <div>Validation must be completed within <strong>30 calendar days</strong> of signal detection. This is a regulatory obligation under Art. 23b of Directive 2001/83/EC.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div>
        <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:13px;margin-bottom:14px;">Validation determines whether the detected signal constitutes a valid safety signal requiring further evaluation — i.e., that the information has not already been assessed, and that there is evidence meeting the signal definition threshold.</p>
        <h4 style="color:var(--accent);font-size:13px;margin-bottom:10px;">Validation Checklist</h4>
        <div class="tbl-wrap">
          <table>
            <tr><th>CRITERIA</th><th>QUESTION</th></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Novelty</strong></td><td>Is this already in the SmPC / RMP?</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Data Sufficiency</strong></td><td>Does the data meet minimum case threshold?</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Case Quality</strong></td><td>Are cases adequately documented?</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Alternative Explanation</strong></td><td>Confounding, coding error, data artefact?</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Biological Plausibility</strong></td><td>Known mechanism or precedent in class?</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Consistency</strong></td><td>Same pattern across multiple data sources?</td></tr>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4 style="color:var(--accent);font-size:13px;margin-bottom:12px;">Validation Decision Tree</h4>
        <div class="dtree">
          <div class="dt-q">Is the drug-event combination already listed in the Reference Safety Information?</div>
          <div class="dt-row">
            <div class="dt-yes">
              <div class="dt-label">✓ YES — LISTED</div>
              <div class="dt-text">Is there evidence of a new aspect (e.g. severity, frequency, special population)? If no → close as NOT a new signal. If yes → proceed to validation of new aspect.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="dt-no">
              <div class="dt-label">✗ NO — UNLISTED</div>
              <div class="dt-text">Proceed to assess data quality and plausibility. Is there sufficient information? If yes → validated signal. If no → request additional information.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="dt-q">Does the signal meet the GVP IX definition threshold?</div>
          <div class="dt-row">
            <div class="dt-yes">
              <div class="dt-label">✓ VALIDATED SIGNAL</div>
              <div class="dt-text">Notify NCA / PRAC (if centrally authorised). Proceed to prioritisation and assessment. Update Signal Tracking System (STS).</div>
            </div>
            <div class="dt-no">
              <div class="dt-label">✗ NOT A SIGNAL</div>
              <div class="dt-text">Document rationale in Signal Log. Close case. Continue routine monitoring. No regulatory action required.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step-detail" id="detail-2">
    <h3>Step 03 — Signal Confirmation & Prioritisation</h3>
    <div class="sub">RESPONSIBILITY: PRAC (centrally authorised) / NCA (nationally authorised) | PRAC Reviews: Monthly</div>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div>
        <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:13px;margin-bottom:14px;">For centrally authorised products, the MAH submits validated signals to EMA/PRAC. PRAC confirms signals and prioritises them at its monthly meeting. For nationally authorised products, signals are confirmed by the relevant NCA and shared through the signal exchange mechanism.</p>
        <h4 style="color:var(--accent);font-size:13px;margin-bottom:10px;">Prioritisation Criteria (GVP IX §C.1.6)</h4>
        <div class="tbl-wrap">
          <table>
            <tr><th>FACTOR</th><th>HIGH PRIORITY INDICATORS</th></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Seriousness</strong></td><td>Fatal/life-threatening, hospitalisation required</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Severity</strong></td><td>Permanent disability, significant incapacity</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Frequency</strong></td><td>High reporting rate relative to exposure</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Population</strong></td><td>Vulnerable groups: paediatric, pregnant, elderly</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Preventability</strong></td><td>Risk reducible by clinical intervention</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Evidence strength</strong></td><td>Multiple independent data sources</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Impact on B/R</strong></td><td>Potential to alter the benefit-risk balance</td></tr>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="alert alert-info">
          <span class="icon">📅</span>
          <div><strong>PRAC Signal Review Cycle:</strong> PRAC examines signal lists submitted by MAHs and NCAs at its monthly plenary meetings. Confirmed signals are assigned for formal assessment or monitoring.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="alert alert-green">
          <span class="icon">📨</span>
          <div><strong>Submission Package:</strong> MAH must provide validated signal notification including: description of detected signal, case narratives, disproportionality data, relevant literature, and proposed assessment timeline.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="alert alert-warn">
          <span class="icon">⚠️</span>
          <div><strong>Urgent Safety Restrictions:</strong> If a signal indicates an imminent risk to public health, MAH must notify the NCA within 24 hours and may be required to issue immediate interim safety measures.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step-detail" id="detail-3">
    <h3>Step 04 — Signal Assessment</h3>
    <div class="sub">RESPONSIBILITY: MAH (initial assessment) + PRAC Rapporteur / NCA | DEADLINE: Varies by priority</div>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div>
        <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:13px;margin-bottom:14px;">A thorough causality and impact assessment reviewing all available data. The output is a Detailed Assessment Report (DAR) that feeds into the PRAC signal assessment process and ultimately informs regulatory recommendations.</p>
        <h4 style="color:var(--accent);font-size:13px;margin-bottom:10px;">Bradford Hill Criteria Application</h4>
        <div class="toggle-item">
          <div class="toggle-head" onclick="tog(this)">1. Strength of Association <span class="chevron">▼</span></div>
          <div class="toggle-body">How large is the relative risk/ROR/PRR? Strong associations (RR>3) are less likely to be due to confounding.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="toggle-item">
          <div class="toggle-head" onclick="tog(this)">2. Consistency <span class="chevron">▼</span></div>
          <div class="toggle-body">Is the association replicated in multiple studies, populations, and data sources (spontaneous, PASS, CTs)?</div>
        </div>
        <div class="toggle-item">
          <div class="toggle-head" onclick="tog(this)">3. Temporality <span class="chevron">▼</span></div>
          <div class="toggle-body">Does exposure precede outcome? What is the time-to-onset distribution? Consistent with pharmacology?</div>
        </div>
        <div class="toggle-item">
          <div class="toggle-head" onclick="tog(this)">4. Dose-Response Relationship <span class="chevron">▼</span></div>
          <div class="toggle-body">Is there evidence of dose-dependent effect? Review cases at different dose levels.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="toggle-item">
          <div class="toggle-head" onclick="tog(this)">5. Biological Plausibility <span class="chevron">▼</span></div>
          <div class="toggle-body">Is there a known or hypothesised mechanism? Is the effect seen with related compounds in the class?</div>
        </div>
        <div class="toggle-item">
          <div class="toggle-head" onclick="tog(this)">6. Dechallenge / Rechallenge <span class="chevron">▼</span></div>
          <div class="toggle-body">Does the event resolve on withdrawal (positive dechallenge)? Does it recur on re-exposure (positive rechallenge)? Positive rechallenge is strong evidence of causality.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4 style="color:var(--accent);font-size:13px;margin-bottom:12px;">WHO-UMC Causality Categories</h4>
        <div class="tbl-wrap">
          <table>
            <tr><th>CATEGORY</th><th>CRITERIA</th></tr>
            <tr><td><strong style="color:var(--green)">Certain</strong></td><td>Plausible time relationship, confirmed on rechallenge, no other explanation</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong style="color:var(--accent)">Probable</strong></td><td>Plausible time relationship, confirmed on dechallenge, alternative explanation unlikely</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong style="color:var(--warn)">Possible</strong></td><td>Plausible time relationship, alternative explanation possible</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong style="color:var(--text-muted)">Unlikely</strong></td><td>Temporal relationship improbable, plausible alternative explanation exists</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong style="color:var(--text-muted)">Conditional</strong></td><td>Event is unusual, more data needed</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong style="color:var(--red)">Unassessable</strong></td><td>Insufficient information to classify</td></tr>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="alert alert-warn">
          <span class="icon">📄</span>
          <div><strong>Assessment Output:</strong> Detailed Assessment Report (DAR) must include benefit-risk impact analysis, proposed label changes, proposed RMP updates, and any additional studies recommended.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step-detail" id="detail-4">
    <h3>Step 05 — Recommendation & Regulatory Action</h3>
    <div class="sub">RESPONSIBILITY: PRAC → CHMP / CMDh → European Commission | Varies by outcome</div>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <div class="card card-accent">
        <h3>📝 SmPC / PIL Update</h3>
        <p>New ADR listed in section 4.8 or warning added in section 4.4. Proposed wording submitted with assessment. MAH issues updated product information via variation procedure.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-warn">
        <h3>📋 RMP Update</h3>
        <p>Safety concern moved from "potential" to "identified risk" category. Additional pharmacovigilance activities (PASS) or risk minimisation measures imposed. Next RMP version required.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-red">
        <h3>🚨 Urgent Safety Restriction</h3>
        <p>Immediate interim measures while formal variation is processed. May include contraindication, dose reduction, or withdrawal from market. NCA or MAH may initiate.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-green">
        <h3>✅ No Action / Close</h3>
        <p>Evidence does not confirm signal. Signal closed with documented rationale. Added to closed signal log. Continue enhanced monitoring at next routine cycle.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-orange">
        <h3>🔬 Additional Study Required</h3>
        <p>PASS/PAES imposed under Article 21a/22a. Protocol must be submitted within defined timeframe. Interim results submitted to PRAC at defined milestones.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>📢 Direct Healthcare Professional Communication (DHPC)</h3>
        <p>When a new safety concern requires urgent communication to prescribers/patients. Coordinated with NCA. Template approved by PRAC/CHMP before distribution.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ DETECTION -->
<section class="section" id="tab-detection">
  <div class="section-title">Operational Training</div>
  <div class="section-h2">Signal Detection — Hands-On Operations</div>
  <div class="section-desc">Step-by-step operational guide for conducting routine signal detection on EudraVigilance and other databases.</div>

  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="card card-accent" style="margin-bottom:0;">
      <h3>🖥️ EudraVigilance Signal Detection — SOP Walkthrough</h3>
      <div class="timeline" style="margin-top:14px;">
        <div class="tl-item">
          <div class="tl-left"><div class="tl-dot"></div><div class="tl-line"></div></div>
          <div class="tl-content">
            <div class="tl-date">Step 1 · Access</div>
            <h4>Log into EV Web Trader Portal</h4>
            <p>Navigate to eudravigilance.ema.europa.eu. Select "Signal Detection" module. Ensure your MAH registration is active.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tl-item">
          <div class="tl-left"><div class="tl-dot"></div><div class="tl-line"></div></div>
          <div class="tl-content">
            <div class="tl-date">Step 2 · Query Configuration</div>
            <h4>Set Product / Substance Filter</h4>
            <p>Select active substance. Apply MedDRA version (current: v26.1). Choose monitoring period (e.g. last 14 days). Select seriousness filter if required.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tl-item">
          <div class="tl-left"><div class="tl-dot warn"></div><div class="tl-line"></div></div>
          <div class="tl-content">
            <div class="tl-date">Step 3 · Run PRR Calculation</div>
            <h4>Apply Disproportionality Statistics</h4>
            <p>Export case counts by PT. Calculate PRR = (n_drug/N_drug) ÷ (n_other/N_other). Flag where PRR≥2, n≥3, χ²≥4.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tl-item">
          <div class="tl-left"><div class="tl-dot warn"></div><div class="tl-line"></div></div>
          <div class="tl-content">
            <div class="tl-date">Step 4 · Case Review</div>
            <h4>Individual Case Narratives</h4>
            <p>Review each flagged case. Record: age/sex, dose, indication, time-to-onset, outcome, dechallenge, concomitant drugs.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tl-item">
          <div class="tl-left"><div class="tl-dot green"></div></div>
          <div class="tl-content">
            <div class="tl-date">Step 5 · Documentation</div>
            <h4>Update Signal Log</h4>
            <p>Record conclusion in Signal Management Log. If signal: initiate validation workflow. Retain all query outputs per GVP IX §C.1.4.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
        <h3>📐 PRR Calculation — Worked Example</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">Drug X — EV Database — Monitoring period: Jan–Mar 2024</p>
        <div class="code-block">
<span class="cm">// EV EXPORT DATA — Drug X — Hepatotoxicity PT</span>
<span class="ck">n_drugX_event</span>   = <span class="cv">18</span>   <span class="cm">// Cases: Drug X + Hepatotoxicity</span>
<span class="ck">N_drugX_total</span>   = <span class="cv">1240</span>  <span class="cm">// All Drug X cases in period</span>
<span class="ck">n_other_event</span>   = <span class="cv">3200</span>  <span class="cm">// Hepatotox in all other drugs</span>
<span class="ck">N_other_total</span>   = <span class="cv">980000</span> <span class="cm">// All other drug cases</span>

<span class="cm">// CALCULATE PRR</span>
PRR = (<span class="cv">18</span>/<span class="cv">1240</span>) ÷ (<span class="cv">3200</span>/<span class="cv">980000</span>)
    = <span class="cv">0.01452</span> ÷ <span class="cv">0.003265</span>
    = <span class="cs">4.45</span>  <span class="cm">← PRR ≥ 2 ✓</span>

<span class="cm">// EVANS CRITERIA CHECK</span>
n (cases)    = <span class="cs">18</span>   <span class="cm">≥ 3  ✓</span>
PRR          = <span class="cs">4.45</span> <span class="cm">≥ 2  ✓</span>
χ² (calc)    = <span class="cs">38.7</span> <span class="cm">≥ 4  ✓</span>

<span class="cm">// RESULT: ⚠️  SIGNAL FLAGGED</span>
<span class="cm">// Action: Proceed to Validation</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-warn">
