    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>📝 DAR Structure — Mandatory Sections</h3>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="tbl-wrap">
        <table>
          <tr><th>#</th><th>SECTION</th><th>KEY CONTENT</th></tr>
          <tr><td>1</td><td><strong>Executive Summary</strong></td><td>Signal description, B/R conclusion, proposed action</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2</td><td><strong>Background</strong></td><td>Product, indication, mechanism, approved population</td></tr>
          <tr><td>3</td><td><strong>Signal Description</strong></td><td>Source, detection method, case characteristics, QSD</td></tr>
          <tr><td>4</td><td><strong>Epidemiology</strong></td><td>Background incidence, exposure estimates, at-risk populations</td></tr>
          <tr><td>5</td><td><strong>Clinical Evidence</strong></td><td>CT data, PASS results, published studies</td></tr>
          <tr><td>6</td><td><strong>Non-Clinical</strong></td><td>Animal toxicology, in vitro mechanistic data</td></tr>
          <tr><td>7</td><td><strong>Causality Assessment</strong></td><td>Bradford Hill criteria applied with case-by-case analysis</td></tr>
          <tr><td>8</td><td><strong>B/R Impact</strong></td><td>Does new risk alter the overall benefit-risk balance?</td></tr>
          <tr><td>9</td><td><strong>Proposed Label Changes</strong></td><td>Specific proposed SmPC/PIL wording</td></tr>
          <tr><td>10</td><td><strong>Proposed RMP Changes</strong></td><td>Safety concern category, risk minimisation measures</td></tr>
          <tr><td>11</td><td><strong>Additional Actions</strong></td><td>PASS/PAES protocol outline, DHPC need, restrictions</td></tr>
          <tr><td>12</td><td><strong>References</strong></td><td>All cited literature, case reports, regulatory documents</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="alert alert-warn">
          <span class="icon">📅</span>
          <div><strong>Assessment Timelines:</strong><br>
          • <strong>Priority signals:</strong> MAH initial assessment within 30 days of PRAC confirmation<br>
          • <strong>Standard signals:</strong> Assessment within 60 days<br>
          • <strong>PRAC response:</strong> 2 PRAC meeting cycles (typically ~2 months)
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="alert alert-green">
          <span class="icon">🏥</span>
          <div><strong>Special Population Consideration:</strong> All DARs must explicitly address whether the signal is relevant in paediatric, geriatric, pregnant, and renally/hepatically impaired populations — even if data are absent.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="alert alert-info">
          <span class="icon">🔗</span>
          <div><strong>RMP Integration:</strong> Every assessed signal must be reconciled with the current RMP. The assessor must conclude whether the safety concern category needs updating and whether existing risk minimisation measures are adequate.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

