    <div class="card card-accent" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
      <h3>📐 Method 1 — Proportional Reporting Ratio (PRR)</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">Evans et al. method — used by MHRA, widely adopted in EU pharmacovigilance</p>
      <div class="code-block">
<span class="cm">// CONTINGENCY TABLE</span>
           Drug X    All other drugs
Event E  :  <span class="ck">a</span>    |    <span class="ck">b</span>
Non-E    :  <span class="ck">c</span>    |    <span class="ck">d</span>

<span class="cm">// FORMULA</span>
PRR = (a/(a+c)) ÷ (b/(b+d))

<span class="cm">// CHI-SQUARE</span>
χ² = (|a - E|² / E)  where E = (a+b)(a+c)/(a+b+c+d)

<span class="cm">// EVANS SIGNAL CRITERIA</span>
✓ PRR  ≥ <span class="cv">2.0</span>
✓ n    ≥ <span class="cv">3</span>  cases
✓ χ²   ≥ <span class="cv">4.0</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
      <h3>📐 Method 2 — Reporting Odds Ratio (ROR)</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">Analogous to odds ratio in case-control studies — used in Netherlands Pharmacovigilance Centre (LAREB)</p>
      <div class="code-block">
<span class="cm">// FORMULA</span>
ROR = (a/c) ÷ (b/d) = (a×d)/(b×c)

<span class="cm">// 95% CONFIDENCE INTERVAL</span>
SE(ln ROR) = √(1/a + 1/b + 1/c + 1/d)
CI_lower = exp(ln(ROR) - 1.96 × SE)
CI_upper = exp(ln(ROR) + 1.96 × SE)

<span class="cm">// SIGNAL THRESHOLD</span>
Signal if: ROR <span class="cv">lower 95% CI</span> > <span class="cv">1.0</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
      <h3>📐 Method 3 — Information Component (IC)</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">Bayesian method — WHO Uppsala Monitoring Centre / VigiBase. Preferred for large databases.</p>
      <div class="code-block">
<span class="cm">// FORMULA (simplified)</span>
IC = log₂(observed / expected)
   = log₂(n_obs / n_exp)

<span class="cm">// n_exp = (N_drug × N_event) / N_total</span>

<span class="cm">// CREDIBILITY INTERVAL</span>
IC025 = lower bound of 95% CI

<span class="cm">// SIGNAL THRESHOLD</span>
Signal if: IC025 > <span class="cv">0</span>
Strong signal: IC > <span class="cv">1.5</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
      <h3>📐 Method 4 — Empirical Bayes (EBGM / EB05)</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">FDA AERS/FAERS method. GPS (Gamma-Poisson Shrinker) / MGPS.</p>
      <div class="code-block">
<span class="cm">// CONCEPT</span>
EBGM: geometric mean of the posterior distribution
      of the relative reporting ratio λ

<span class="cm">// KEY METRIC</span>
EB05: lower 5th percentile — conservative threshold

<span class="cm">// FDA SIGNAL THRESHOLD</span>
Signal if: EB05 ≥ <span class="cv">2.0</span>

<span class="cm">// ADVANTAGE</span>
Shrinks noisy estimates for rare drug-event pairs
Reduces false positive rate vs. PRR
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>⚖️ Method Comparison — When to Use Each</h3>
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table>
        <tr>
          <th>METHOD</th>
          <th>DATABASE</th>
          <th>THRESHOLD</th>
          <th>ADVANTAGE</th>
          <th>LIMITATION</th>
          <th>GVP IX USE</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>PRR (Evans)</strong></td>
          <td>EudraVigilance, Yellow Card</td>
          <td>≥2, n≥3, χ²≥4</td>
          <td>Simple, transparent, easy to audit</td>
          <td>Unstable for small n; no shrinkage</td>
          <td>✅ Primary EU method</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>ROR</strong></td>
          <td>LAREB, national DBs</td>
          <td>Lower 95% CI >1</td>
          <td>Confidence intervals included</td>
          <td>Inflated with small cells</td>
          <td>✅ Supplementary</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>IC / IC025</strong></td>
          <td>VigiBase (WHO)</td>
          <td>IC025 >0</td>
          <td>Bayesian shrinkage; handles large DB</td>
          <td>Interpretation less intuitive</td>
          <td>✅ Cross-validation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>EBGM / EB05</strong></td>
          <td>FDA FAERS</td>
          <td>EB05 ≥2</td>
          <td>Best for rare events, reduces FP</td>
          <td>Complex computation</td>
          <td>ℹ️ Cross-reference</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Observed vs Expected</strong></td>
          <td>All sources</td>
          <td>O/E ratio >1</td>
          <td>Epidemiologically grounded</td>
          <td>Requires background incidence data</td>
          <td>✅ PASS/PAES analysis</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

</section>

